module gunbc.plans.one_source_tree

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, quote }

fn one_source_tree_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`): what the repository should become, why, and done-when, with the design the target state must satisfy. The work items that realize it are roadmap nodes under `one-source-tree`, each naming this intention; their order and slices live there, not here."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` (a second place that decides one meaning is a fork; the name-to-path mapping is a single authority that runs one way), `gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy`, `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` (the old authority ends at its root, in one motion), `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` (every caller that restates the roots is one family), and the operator's file-less direction, `gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded`. The ruling this plan carries is `gunbc.design_ruling::one_source_tree_and_the_v2_namespace_dissolves`."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** gunbc's `.dag` source is one tree, `dag/`, under one storage rule, and `v2` stops being a concept that source is organized by. Nothing is named `v2.*`; every concept the `v2.*` modules carry has one home beside the concepts it duplicates or extends. A person running gunbc names what they want by its declaration path and never names a directory, a tree or a source file."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-22):** the two trees were not intended -- \"i didn't intent for things to sprawl this much (basically a duplicate authority issue)\" -- and the way they diverge is not understood. The split is not a boundary: imports run both ways (section 2), so `src/v2` is one program stored in a second place, and its `v2.std` and `v2.extdeps` hold second declarations of concepts `std` and `extdeps` already own, `Int` among them. Every caller restates the split by hand as `--source-root dag --source-root src/v2`, and a caller that forgets one root fails at run time (the shadow-gate remote steps, 2026-11-22). And the operator is \"trying to get away from filepaths/filesystem stuff for users\": a source root is a filesystem fact the user is made to supply."),
    p(text: "**Done when** (each assessed against the tree unless marked as the operator's judgement):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "No `.dag` file is stored under `src/v2/`, and `gunbc.source_layout` declares one governed tree, `dag`, with no namespace row: module `a.b.c` is stored at `dag/a/b/c.dag` for every `a`."),
      li(text: "No module is named `v2` or `v2.*` (the `module` line of every governed file), and no source imports one."),
      li(text: "Every same-named or same-concept pair the survey of section 2 found between `v2.std` and `std`, and between `v2.extdeps` and `extdeps`, is resolved: one declaration for one concept, or a rename that says the two are different concepts. The pair list is a candidate set read by `git grep`, not a census; a pair found later is reconciled when found."),
      li(text: "No cross-tree machinery remains: `v2.std.cross_tree` and the active-root denials in name resolution are deleted, each with its discriminating controls kept enrolled against the one-tree layout (a namespace no layout row declares still refuses)."),
      li(text: "No committed caller passes `--source-root` or names an entry by file path: workflow generators, scripts, instrument rows, the remote-build client and server, and comments that quote a command. The CLI grammar has neither option, nor an environment variable standing in for one; a command run from any directory inside the checkout resolves the same source."),
      li(text: "The workspace is a root manifest: a `.dag` declaration that holds the trees, the namespaces and the composed workspaces, read by both the seed and the native CLI; `gunbc.source_layout`'s policy and `gunbc.layout_namespace_row`'s rows are its content, not a second copy beside it. A repository composed with gunbc names gunbc in its own manifest, by name and revision, and no gate copies its tree."),
      li(text: "Every consumer section 4a lists has its stated answer realized, the test harness first, each with a control that runs it without a root argument."),
      li(text: "DESIGN.md's single-authority claim states the one-tree rule (it is regenerated from `gunbc.design_argument`, never hand-edited)."),
      li(text: "Operator's judgement: someone reading the repository for the first time sees one tree and one standard library, and can run a declaration without knowing where it is stored."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. Observation, 2026-11-22 at 00de8d4c88da"),
    p(text: "Producers: `find`, `comm` and `git grep` over the checkout at that revision, run by session gentle-stag-778. Text search finds candidates, not semantic absence."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Population.** `src/v2` holds 1,856 `.dag` files and 35 `.txt` fixtures: test 1,351, std 121, compiler 104, lens 103, workflow 92, extdeps 75, cli 9, native_lane_fixture 1, plus `program.dag`. `dag/v2` does not exist, and every `src/v2` module is named `v2.*`, so moving `src/v2/x/y.dag` to `dag/v2/x/y.dag` renames no module."),
      li(text: "**Imports run both ways.** From `src/v2`: 4,338 imports of `std.*`, 405 of `extdeps.*`, 193 of `gunbc.*`. Into `v2.*` from `dag/`: 480 files (231 under `test/claim`; the rest in instruments, fleet, runner, ci, scm, host, rung_drop), mostly `v2.std` (547 import lines) and `v2.workflow` (207). `gunbc.design_ruling::cross_tree_admission_is_namespace_membership` already measured one 23-namespace import cycle spanning both trees."),
      li(text: "**Families with no counterpart in `dag/`:** `v2.compiler`, `v2.lens`, `v2.workflow`, `v2.cli`. `v2.test` has none at file grain (0 shared paths with `test`, though both have claim, fixture and manual directories)."),
      li(text: "**Families that duplicate a `dag/` concept.** `v2.std` beside `std`: 10 shared stems (change, coercion, determinism, effects, emit_on_demand, integer, logic, nat, node, verification) and 18 type names declared in both: Int, UInt, Int8 to Int128, UInt8 to UInt128, IntPlatform, UIntPlatform, NonNegativeInt, PositiveInt, TerminationProof, Unit. The sharpest is `Int`: `std.integer::Int` is `NonNegative { n: Nat } | Negative { pred: Nat }`, `v2.std.integer` declares `Int = GroupCompletion<Nat>`; 219 files import `v2.std.integer` and 326 import `std.integer`. Most shared stems are different concepts under one stem (`v2.std.node` is the 3,404-line compiler tree; `std.node` is 122 lines with no shared declaration name). `v2.extdeps` beside `extdeps`: no shared file, 5 shared directories (bmc, cache, formats, github, languages) and 7 shared type names: Component, Filesystem, GoFloatWidth, SqlDialect, SqlMigrationEmissionTarget, SqlMigrationScript, SqlMigrationStep. `v2.extdeps.file_system` Filesystem beside `extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io`, the effect service the native route admits, is the one to read first."),
      li(text: "**References to the path.** 4,558 occurrences of `src/v2` in 1,061 tracked files: about 4,990 `src/v2/....dag` path strings (about 580 on comment lines), and 840 root-passing occurrences (`--source-root ... src/v2` or the literal `\"src/v2\"`) in 409 files. Concentrations: `.github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml` 143 (generated; fixed at its generator), the seed's `cli_run.rs` 78, `required_regen_host.rs` 23, `cssl_seed_linked_closure_assembly.rs` 13, `native_lane_runner.rs` 12, and `gunbc.instrument_targets`."),
      li(text: "**Where the two-tree rule is written.** `gunbc.source_layout` (`LayoutTreeV2`, the `v2` namespace row with `elides_namespace: true`, `layout_governed_roots`); its consumers `v2.cli.repository_layout` and `v2.compiler.source_authority`; `gunbc.generated_artifact_dispatch_equivalence` (routes by tree prefix); `gunbc.required_ci_contract_epoch` (hashes the layout, so the change is a deliberate epoch bump); the seed's own copy, `src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/source_layout_lookup.rs`, which renders `src/v2/...` and asserts the policy text; and fixtures spelling the two-tree layout (`V2Tree` rows, 102 in `v2.test.fixture.frontier_probe_elision_boundary_overlay` alone)."),
      li(text: "**Outside the repository or historical.** The pinned remote-build copies on srv1, srv3 and srv4; repositories that compose their `dag/` beside gunbc's (`gunbc.layout_namespace_row` rows carry a repository); dated records (`handoff/2026-11-08/*`, `artifacts/rung-drops/*`), which are history and are not rewritten."),
      li(text: "**Not in scope:** `src/v1/*.dag` (48 files, `module v1.*`), the seed's own stages. The layout leaves them outside the governed roots by design, and they retire with the seed."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "3. The target layout"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**One tree, one rule.** `gunbc.source_layout` keeps the policy shape but loses its special case: no `LayoutTreeV2`, no namespace row, `layout_governed_roots` is `[\"dag\"]`. Whether `LayoutTree` keeps one arm or is deleted is decided by its consumers at the cut; a one-arm type kept only for shape is dead structure."),
      li(text: "**The move renames no module.** The first cut stores `v2.x.y` at `dag/v2/x/y.dag`: the same names, one tree. Every later rename (section 5) moves a file inside `dag/` and changes its name, never its tree."),
      li(text: "**Cross-tree admission dissolves.** With one tree there is no crossing, so `v2.std.cross_tree` and the active-root denials have nothing to decide. Their RED controls stay as regression controls re-pointed at what still refuses: a module in a namespace no layout row declares, and a duplicate storage path."),
      li(text: "**One motion** (`gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`, precedent `gunbc.source_layout_rulings` R7). A half-moved tree is a dual representation R3 forbids, so the layout change, the file move, every root-passing caller and the seed's lookup land together, with the required job and heal green on the result. Callers outside the required gate are enumerated by name before the cut (section 2 is the starting list), and the pinned remote-build hosts are updated immediately after it."),
      li(text: "**The seed changes only where the cut mechanically requires it** (R8 precedent): `source_layout_lookup.rs` and the hard-coded roots in `cli_run.rs` and its neighbours. The seed keeps its whole-tree read; reading one tree instead of two is the same read."),
      li(text: "**DESIGN.md.** The single-authority claim's name-to-path paragraph and the cross-tree sentence change in `gunbc.design_argument` in the same change, and DESIGN.md is regenerated from it."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Naming without paths: the workspace manifest replaces --source-root"),
    p(text: "A source root is two facts made into one argument: which repository the user means, and where in it source is stored. The second is already modeled (`gunbc.source_layout`), so a caller passing it is a second copy of the layout, and the first is where the command was run. The design follows the universe ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded`): source enters at one ingest step as a bundle, and everything after it is named. This section designs the boundary the user touches; making stages after ingest file-free is `universe-ingest-replaces-file-acquisition` under `gunbc.plans.v2_self_host`, and neither waits on the other."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**A workspace is declared by its root manifest** (ruling (e), as Bazel's workspace root and module file are). The manifest is one `.dag` declaration at the checkout's root, the entry point for everything the checkout holds: which trees it stores source in, which namespaces it declares, which other workspaces it composes, and the defaults that flags carry today. The command finds it by walking up from the working directory to the nearest directory holding the manifest; that one fixed file name is the only path convention left, as `MODULE.bazel` is Bazel's. Outside any workspace the command refuses with a typed cause naming the directory it searched from. This replaces the `.git`-ancestor walk and `GUNBC_WORKSPACE_ROOT`, recorded as a scaffold in `gunbc.cli_run_workspace_root_scaffold`; an environment variable naming a root is the same flag in another channel."),
      li(text: "**The layout is the manifest's content, not a second authority.** `gunbc.source_layout` today holds the storage policy and `gunbc.layout_namespace_row` one namespace row per repository. After this they are what the manifest declares: the manifest's type owns the storage rule's parameters (one tree, `dag`) and its namespace rows, and the compiler reads them from the manifest it found. Because the manifest must be readable before the layout is known, it imports only `std`, and its home is decided by the first slice: a `std` type if it is the language's notion of a workspace, a gunbc module otherwise. Its name is decided there too: `workspace` already means a provisioned developer slot (`gunbc.workspace_allocation`) and a repository's untracked footprint (`gunbc.repo_workspace`), so reusing it would be a meaning fork (`gunbc.design_argument::single_authority`)."),
      li(text: "**The bundle is derived from the manifest.** The source the command ingests is the manifest's trees plus those of the workspaces it composes. No caller states it, so no caller can drop part of it."),
      li(text: "**Flags become declarations** (ruling (e), extending `gunbc.design_ruling::instrument_is_a_row_not_a_flag`). What a flag says today is either a fact of the workspace (its trees: in the manifest), a fact of the thing run (its memory envelope, which producer realizes it: a row on the declaration the user names, as instrument rows already are), or a choice the user makes at this invocation (the declarations to run, the execution mode that permits live effects as `gunbc.plans.claim_execution_consolidation` keeps it, an output location). Only the third stays on the command line, and the user names the declaration, never its file."),
      li(text: "**The user names a declaration.** `gunbc run <declaration path>` replaces `--entry <file> --function <name>`: `gunbc run gunbc.design_ruling.expected_design_rulings_md`. The path is spelled the way `std.decl_ref`'s display key spells it when this lands; `one-declaration-identity-carrier` is moving that rendering to dots, and the CLI accepts exactly one spelling, never both. Claim runs: `gunbc.plans.claim_execution_consolidation` keeps the `gunbc test` label grammar as the durable caller interface. A `//test/claim/<pkg>:<stem>` label spells a module path with the tree's directory shape, so it is already close to a declaration path; whether it becomes one is decided jointly with that plan, not by this one (section 7)."),
      li(text: "**Paths remain only where the user reads them.** A diagnostic still shows file and line beside the declaration path, from the ingest step's text mapping (the one place the universe ruling keeps files). An output location (`--output-dir`) is a separate filesystem fact and is out of scope here."),
      li(text: "**Fixture workspaces are workspaces.** A control that runs the CLI over a scratch layout gives that layout its own manifest and runs inside it, so no test-only root flag survives into the user's grammar; a root flag kept for harnesses is the escape hatch `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` rejects. A control that does not spawn the CLI hands its universe to the ingest step as a value, not a path. Each consumer's answer is in section 4a."),
      li(text: "**Composed repositories are workspaces the manifest names** (ruling (e)). Today a repository with `.dag` modules and no compiler is checked by gunbc's gate with its `dag/` copied beside gunbc's and its own namespace row file (`gunbc.layout_namespace_row`, `gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow`'s called form). Under the manifest the direction is the dependency's: that repository's manifest declares its own namespaces and names gunbc as a workspace it composes, by name and pinned revision, never by path, the way a Bazel module names a `bazel_dep` with its lockfile. Fetching a composed workspace into a local store is realization the command performs, not a fact the user supplies. A local override for developing two repositories together is a row in the manifest, the one place a path may be written, and never a flag. Composition is by namespace: a namespace declared by two composed workspaces refuses at ingest, naming both."),
      li(text: "**Ordering with the cut.** The manifest lands first as a model (its type and gunbc's own manifest, read by nothing yet), then the callers stop passing roots, then the cut. Deriving the roots before the cut shrinks it: once no caller passes roots, the cut changes the manifest's tree row, not 409 files of arguments."),
      li(text: "**The seed CLI changes** (ruling (f)). The seed's `gunbc run` and claim batch drop `--source-root` and the entry-file flag and read the manifest. This is a v1 change admitted by the operator under `gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing`; it is bounded to the CLI boundary and the lookup, and the seed keeps its whole-tree read."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4a. Every consumer of source roots, and its answer"),
    p(text: "Ruling (g): each consumer is named and given its answer before the flags go. Producer: `git grep` for `--source-root`, `--entry`, `--functions`, `--hermetic` and the root-building symbols across `dag/`, `src/v2/`, `src/v1/`, `.github/`, `docs/`, `tools/`, `fixtures/`, `.githooks/` at 00de8d4c88da, run by a survey agent of session gentle-stag-778; counts are matching lines, not a census, and `apps/`, `sites/`, `provider-runtime/`, `handoff/` and the Rust tests' bodies were not read. About 2,200 matching lines trace to the authorities below, so most of the change is at a few roots and the rest is regeneration."),
    p(text: "**The test harness, first.**"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Instrument targets.** `gunbc test <label>` reaches `src/v1/stage0/src/target_invocation_host.rs` `run_producer`, which takes roots from `gunbc.instrument_targets` `instrument_source_roots_rows` (generated into `instrument_registry_generated.rs`), from `cli_run::default_source_roots()` and from three hard-coded `[\"dag\", \"src/v2\"]` lists. Answer: the per-target root rows are deleted; every target runs in the workspace its manifest declares. The one target with a different universe, `bare_reference_channel` (`fixtures/bare_reference_channel`), names a fixture workspace (below), not a directory."),
      li(text: "**Producer entries.** `gunbc.target_binding` `TargetProducer` (102 bindings) carries `entry: String` as a file path on its CLI-wire, native-claim and native-serve producers. Answer: the field becomes a `std.decl_ref` `DeclarationRef`; the producer resolves it in the workspace."),
      li(text: "**Claim batches and witness binaries.** `gunbc.instruments.host_prelude` `claim_batch_claims_argv_route` and `run_gunbc_claims(source_roots, claims)` (callers such as `cheap_gate_pool`) pass roots; the seed's `claim_batch.rs` parses `--source-root`, `--entry`, `--function(s)` and `--hermetic`. Answer: `gunbc.plans.claim_execution_consolidation` already deletes `claim_batch` and `gunbc run --claim-run`, so every claim caller reaches `gunbc test` with an exact batch of operands, and its execution mode (`std.execution_mode::ExecutionMode`) stays an invocation option, because permitting live effects is the caller's choice at that run, the third kind of flag in section 4. This plan consumes that cutover rather than restating it: `harness-runs-in-the-workspace` waits on `claim-entrypoints-cutover`, and then removes roots from the one surviving entrypoint. That plan's done-when \"no silent change of source universe\" (each caller's roots classified as redundant with `witness_layer_roots` or meaningful) is the classification this section's fixture answers act on: a redundant set is deleted, a meaningful one becomes a fixture manifest. The `source_roots` parameter is deleted rather than defaulted."),
      li(text: "**Claims that spell argv literally** (about 85 files under `dag/test/claim`, 29 under `src/v2/test/claim`, e.g. `typed_witness_invocation`). Answer: they build their invocation through the one argv authority below, so they change when it does; a claim that asserts the old flag grammar is re-pointed to assert the new grammar's refusal of `--source-root` as an unknown option."),
      li(text: "**Fixture workspaces with their own universe.** About 45 `fixtures/*` trees (some already nested, `fixtures/native_cli_door`), 16 tests that pass a `mktemp` directory as a second root (`claim_batch_exit_two_unobserved_witness`), and about 21 seed Rust tests that build temporary workspaces. Answer: each is a workspace with its own manifest, and runs inside it; discovery takes the nearest manifest, so a nested fixture is found before the checkout. A fixture that needs gunbc's `std` composes the enclosing workspace by a typed manifest row meaning the enclosing workspace, not a relative path. The two recorded refusals for extra roots (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::extra_source_root_outside_workspace_refuses_annotations_as_unattached`, `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::absolute_extra_source_root_panics_instead_of_typed_refusal`) lose their invalid state, since there is no extra root to pass; their REDs are re-pointed at a manifest that composes a workspace it cannot find."),
      li(text: "**Narrowed pools inside the universe.** 10 witnesses narrow the pool to a subtree of `dag/test/fixture`, and fact intrinsics take `pool_roots:` (119 files, mostly `[\"dag\"]` or `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` `witness_layer_roots`). These narrow within one universe rather than replace it. Answer: the argument becomes a namespace selection (module path prefixes, such as `test.fixture.module_graph`), never a directory; an intrinsic that reads the whole universe takes no argument."),
      li(text: "**Fixtures already built as values.** `AcquisitionEnv { layout, bindings }` in `v2.compiler.module_acquisition`, used in memory by its claims, and the name-resolution wall's supplied trees need no change: they already hand the ingest step a universe. `AcquisitionEnv.bindings` is the seam the manifest resolves to, and `host_directory` stays inside ingest, the one place the universe ruling keeps files. The `V2Tree` fixture rows go with the cut."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Everyone else.**"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**The one argv authority.** `gunbc.cli_invoke` (`source_root_transport_argv`, `source_roots_shell_flags`, `gunbc_run_invocation_words`, `gunbc_run_transport_argv`) over `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` `witness_layer_roots`, which 106 files import and which is a second copy of the layout. Answer: the root words are deleted from `gunbc.cli_invoke` and `witness_layer_roots` is deleted; its importers take the workspace or a namespace selection."),
      li(text: "**Generated workflows.** `v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit` `gunbc_run_command` and the generators `gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow`, `gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow`, `gunbc.heal_publisher_workflow`, the drift-watch and branch-run-grant generators, and `gunbc.heal_workflow`, whose `heal.yml` spells the roots literally. Answer: changed at the generators and regenerated in the same change; no `.yml` is edited by hand."),
      li(text: "**Heal and the githook.** `claim_executor --regen-round-cost` with roots in `.githooks/generated-artifact-merge` and the seed's `bin/claim_executor.rs`. Answer: same as the harness; the hook is a generated artifact and is regenerated."),
      li(text: "**Remote build and compute.** `gunbc.compute.work_provider_local` `compute_command_argv` builds roots and an entry file under the checkout; `gunbc.compute.remote_build`'s wire carries `entry: FilePath`, admitted by a `dag/` prefix rule, and `gunbc.compute.remote_build_serve` builds the forced command. Answer: the wire carries a declaration path and the server runs in the snapshot's workspace. The wire is a gap-intolerant boundary between a client and pinned servers, so it takes the staged form of `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`: the servers accept the new request, the client switches, the file-path request is deleted. The same change gives a failed run's receipt its claim verdicts (raised with the remote-build owner on 2026-11-22)."),
      li(text: "**The seed.** `main.rs`'s clap `--source-root` and `entry`, `run_verb`'s no-root refusal, and `cli_run.rs`'s discovery (`workspace_root_from`, `workspace_root_resolve`, `try_resolve_process_workspace_root`, which requires `Cargo.toml` and `dag/`, `declared_workspace_root_from`, `bind_process_workspace_root`, `GUNBC_WORKSPACE_ROOT`), plus tree names hard-coded in about 36 files (`source_layout_lookup.rs`, `demand_acquire.rs`, `rostered_row_join.rs`, `required_regen_host.rs`, `native_lane_runner.rs`, `memory_governor.rs`, `pre_push.rs` and others). Answer (ruling (f)): one discovery function that finds the manifest, every other site reading the trees from it; the release locus requires a manifest instead of `dag/` and a tree receipt. This is a v1 change bounded to the CLI boundary, discovery and the lookup."),
      li(text: "**The native CLI.** `v2.cli.compile_cli` and `v2.cli.source_root_bindings` parse `--source-root`; `emit --entry` already takes a module path. Answer: the same discovery, implemented once in `.dag` and read by the seed's copy only until the seed retires."),
      li(text: "**Docs and quoted commands.** `gunbc.contributor_onboarding_path` `source_root_flags`, seven `docs/` runbooks and plans, two `tools/*.sh`, and quoted commands in live rows (`recurring_failure_mode`, `instruments`, `roadmap`, `integration_concern`). Answer: live text is updated in the change that alters the grammar; dated receipts and handoffs are history and are not rewritten."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "5. Dissolving the v2 namespace"),
    p(text: "After the cut every `v2.*` module sits in `dag/v2/`. The namespace is dissolved family by family, each family one reconciliation (`gunbc.design_argument::continuous_generalization`: the newcomer and the incumbent each account for the other's valid obligations; neither wins for having arrived first)."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Uncontested families are renamed.** `v2.compiler`, `v2.lens`, `v2.workflow`, `v2.cli` and `v2.test` have no counterpart to reconcile against, so dissolving them is a rename and an import rewrite. Proposed names, decided when the family is cut: `compiler.*`, `lens.*` (or `compiler.lens.*` if its consumers are only the compiler), `workflow.*`, `cli.*`, and `test.*` merged into the existing `test` namespace (0 shared file paths). `v2.program` and `v2.native_lane_fixture` go where their single consumers put them. DESIGN.md already treats `compiler` and `workflow` as browsing folders, not authorities."),
      li(text: "**`v2.std` is reconciled into `std`.** This is the existing work item `one-standard-library` (owner self-host, serving `gunbc.plans.v2_self_host`), which already states the rule: the same concept collapses to one declaration; the same carrier in a different role gets a role wrapper; a different concern is renamed into the compiler's namespace so it is not called the language's standard type. This plan consumes that item rather than restating it. The `Int` pair is its first slice; the other 17 shared type names and 10 shared stems are its population."),
      li(text: "**`v2.extdeps` is reconciled into `extdeps`.** Each module is either an upstream fact whose home is an existing `extdeps` module (moved and merged there, its upstream cited, `gunbc.design_argument::external_upstreams`), or a compiler-internal shape misfiled as an upstream (renamed into the compiler's namespace). `Filesystem` first: one service declaration for the filesystem the native route admits."),
      li(text: "**Names collide only at full path.** Under the universe ruling a declaration is identified by its full path, so `compiler.node.String` and `std.text.String` are distinct without an import deciding between them. A rename that produces a full path already declared is a refusal at ingest, never a silent merge. `gunbc.plans.names_without_imports` owns the binding rule; a rename here is a new path for an existing declaration and adds no binding mechanism."),
      li(text: "**The layout's last special case goes with the last family.** When no `v2.*` module remains, nothing about `v2` is left in `gunbc.source_layout` or in any fixture's layout rows."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. Rulings this intention rests on"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "`gunbc.design_ruling::one_source_tree_and_the_v2_namespace_dissolves` (2026-11-22): (a) one tree, `dag`; (b) the `v2` namespace dissolves; (c) the move first, `src/v1` out of scope; (d) it integrates with the rulings it touches and forks none; (e) a workspace is a root manifest, composition is by manifest, and flags become `.dag` declarations; (f) the seed CLI change is admitted; (g) every source-root consumer is worked through by name. It amends `gunbc.source_layout_rulings` R5 and, when the cut lands, supersedes `gunbc.design_ruling::cross_tree_admission_is_namespace_membership`."),
      li(text: "`gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded` (2026-11-17): the bundle-and-universe direction section 4 follows; the manifest declares the bundle that ruling ingests."),
      li(text: "`gunbc.design_ruling::instrument_is_a_row_not_a_flag` (2026-09-16): extended from instruments to every flag that names source or a run's policy."),
      li(text: "`gunbc.source_layout_rulings` R3 (one storage convention, no dual representations), R7 (a layout migration is one PR) and R8 (v1 changes limited to what the cutover mechanically requires) are reused as precedent for the cut."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "7. Open questions"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**The manifest's home and name.** A `std` type or a gunbc module, and a name that is not `workspace` (section 4). Decided by the manifest's first slice."),
      li(text: "**Lockfile.** Whether a composed workspace's pinned revision lives in the manifest or in a separate generated lock, as Bazel's `MODULE.bazel.lock`. Decided when the first composed repository moves to the manifest."),
      li(text: "**Claim and instrument labels.** Whether the `gunbc test` label (kept by `gunbc.plans.claim_execution_consolidation`) becomes a declaration path, reconciled with that plan rather than decided here. Instrument labels: `//gunbc/instruments:self-host` is namespace-shaped already; whether it becomes a declaration path like claims, or stays a label in `gunbc.instrument_targets`, is decided with the claim addressing."),
      li(text: "**The word v2 elsewhere.** Plan and node names (`gunbc.plans.v2_self_host`, `v2-compiler-live`) name the compiler generation, not the namespace. They are out of scope here and retire with the seed, when there is no second generation to tell apart."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data one_source_tree_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "one-source-tree",
  title: "One source tree: dag/ is the only tree, the v2 namespace dissolves, and users name declarations, not paths",
  body: one_source_tree_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 1 is achieved: every done-when condition holds on the tree, and the operator has accepted the judgement condition.") },
}
